From: mscharged-port contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Reset the consumed GX FIFO prefix without a join
Upstream-base: d664382f57002fbff143911c81b06b7e7a4b3ab4
Classification: host performance, no behaviour change.

The FIFO buffer is append-only between drains. In native recording nothing
drained it except the host's full sync at 64 MiB, which joins the processor and
its GPU waits: with 1.2-1.9 MiB of commands per frame that dropped a frame
about once a second in matches, and a long backlog stalled for up to ~450 ms.
rebase_if_caught_up() drops the already processed bytes as drain() does after
its join, but never waits: when everything is processed the buffer resets; when
only a small published tail (at most 4 MiB) is still being processed after an
8 MiB processed prefix, that tail moves to the front. It requires every written
byte to be published (no open primitive or pending patch offset) and runs on
the owner outside display lists; the processor takes the same buffer lock for
every chunk and derives its offset from the stream base inside it.
VIWaitForRetrace calls it after its genuine retrace; hosts may call it between
frames. The full drain remains as the fallback. Apply after 0071.
diff --git a/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp b/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp
index 7d9f92b..9ab1c6e 100644
--- a/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp
+++ b/lib/dolphin/vi/vi.cpp
@@ -534,6 +534,11 @@ void VIWaitForRetrace() {
   // this completed native wait boundary, after the genuine source retrace.
   // Preserve the caller's original saved interrupt state through the mask.
   OSEnableInterrupts(); aurora_service_hardware(); OSDisableInterrupts();
+#ifdef AURORA_ENABLE_GX
+  // The finished frame's commands are usually all processed by now. Reset the
+  // FIFO buffer here instead of letting it grow to the host's full-drain limit.
+  aurora::gx::fifo::rebase_if_caught_up();
+#endif
 }
 u32 VIGetRetraceCount() { auto& state = State(); std::lock_guard lock(state.mutex); RequireOwner(state); return state.retraces; }
 u32 VIGetNextField() {
diff --git a/lib/gx/fifo.cpp b/lib/gx/fifo.cpp
index 80b818c..d7ab4ec 100644
--- a/lib/gx/fifo.cpp
+++ b/lib/gx/fifo.cpp
@@ -416,6 +416,32 @@ void drain() {
   sPendingDraws = 0;
 }
 
+bool rebase_if_caught_up() noexcept {
+  if (sOwner != std::this_thread::get_id() || detail::sInDisplayList || detail::sBufferSize == 0) return false;
+  const uint64_t end = sStreamBase + detail::sBufferSize;
+  // Unpublished bytes (an open primitive with a pending patch offset) stay put.
+  if (sPublished.load(std::memory_order_acquire) != end) return false;
+  // The processor takes this lock for every chunk and derives its read offset
+  // from sStreamBase inside it, so moving the buffer here is consistent.
+  std::lock_guard lock{sBufferMutex};
+  const uint64_t processed = sProcessed.load(std::memory_order_acquire);
+  if (processed == end) {
+    sStreamBase = end;
+    detail::sBufferSize = 0;
+    sPendingDraws = 0;
+    return true;
+  }
+  // A frame tail still being processed: once the processed prefix dominates,
+  // move the small published tail to the front instead of growing the buffer.
+  constexpr uint64_t kMinimumPrefix = 8u << 20, kMaximumTail = 4u << 20;
+  const uint64_t prefix = processed - sStreamBase, tail = end - processed;
+  if (prefix < kMinimumPrefix || tail > kMaximumTail) return false;
+  std::memmove(detail::sBufferData, detail::sBufferData + prefix, tail);
+  sStreamBase = processed;
+  detail::sBufferSize = static_cast<uint32_t>(tail);
+  return true;
+}
+
 const uint8_t* get_buffer_data() { return detail::sBufferData; }
 uint32_t get_buffer_size() { return detail::sBufferSize; }
 
diff --git a/lib/gx/fifo.hpp b/lib/gx/fifo.hpp
index db02fe3..4e8f91a 100644
--- a/lib/gx/fifo.hpp
+++ b/lib/gx/fifo.hpp
@@ -118,6 +118,12 @@ bool in_display_list();
 // Ensure all buffered commands have been processed.
 void drain();
 
+// Owner thread, outside primitives and display lists: drop the bytes the
+// processor has already consumed, as drain() does after its join, without
+// waiting (a small unprocessed tail moves to the front). Returns whether the
+// buffer shrank.
+bool rebase_if_caught_up() noexcept;
+
 // Internal buffer inspection
 const uint8_t* get_buffer_data();
 uint32_t get_buffer_size();
